  "question": {
    "text": "An electron and proton are separated by a large distance. The electron starts approaching the proton with energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>. The proton captures the electrons and forms a hydrogen atom in second excited state. The resulting photon is incident on a photosensitive metal of threshold wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4000</mn><mi>A</mi></math> What is the maximum kinetic energy of the emitted photoelectron?",
    "image": null
  },
